---
# The shape of vault/deploy.yml, which the fix-* playbooks load. The real file
# holds the deploy account's credential and lives only in the private working
# repository - never here, not even encrypted, because a published vault is an
# invitation to attack the passphrase offline.
#
# Create the real one without the plaintext ever touching disk:
#   EDITOR=nano ansible-vault create vault/deploy.yml
# then paste the two lines below with real values, and store the vault
# passphrase in a password manager.
deploy_user: svc-ansible-rw
deploy_password: CHANGE_ME
